chnically breaks compat if a user performs a normalize on non-finite, but I think this is acceptable.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116427#pullrequestreview-3909847739","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116427","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2026-03-07T21:39:49Z"},{"id":3911112936,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7pHtjo","state":"APPROVED","commit_id":"db90de4dbdbe22143df38218e237e688c1db560d","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?u=2b8b17ce969861380874563b333a546e0bbaab56&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","login":"lawnjelly","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly"},"body":"As ever with these kind of checks, it's probably also worth considering whether to have `WARN_PRINT` or `WARN_PRINT_ONCE` here, as if you have 1 bad plane, you've probably got 1000. Although if the error toaster can combine these errors efficiently it's not so bad.\n\nI guess that is the kind of problem that will show up with use though.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116427#pullrequestreview-3911112936","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116427","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2026-03-08T07:22:34Z"}]